<title>SPAIN: Repsol sees positive effects from euro.</title>
<headline>Repsol sees positive effects from euro.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The entry of Spain into monetary union &quot;will only have positive effects on Repsol,&quot; the chairman of the energy group said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In a meeting with journalists ahead of tomorrow's shareholders' meeting, Alfonso Cortina highlighted the sound situation of the firm's chemical division, which he said is more competitive than other European producers.</p>
<p>The deregulation of petrol, liquid petroleum gas (LPG) and natural gas price-capping systems would also be positive for the company, he said.</p>
<p>Cortina forecast that LPG prices will rise towards European levels once the single currency is launched, adding that the price here is currently 71 pesetas per kg while the European average is 161 pesetas per kg.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
